From d13692a3e2550888c4e4f53f833703a79a6032c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] feat(control-plane): add dependency-free Prometheus
 metrics primitives

The control plane has no way to expose metrics: observability.py only
keeps values in memory and nothing scrapes them. Add counters, gauges
and histograms that render the Prometheus text format 0.0.4 using the
standard library only, so no new dependency is needed.

Label cardinality is bounded twice: callers only pass bounded label
values, and each metric caps its series (default 200); new label sets
beyond the cap are counted under an all-"overflow" series so totals
stay correct. Gauges are replaced by collectors at scrape time, and a
failing collector clears its gauges instead of exporting stale values.
Updates are locked because registry calls run on worker threads.

The tests include a strict exposition parser that later tests reuse.
